  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Fabrication of ablative and erosion-resistant nozzles for solid rocket motors. Carbon-carbon composite throats withstand 2,500-3,500 C gas temperatures at the convergent throat; graphite entrance and exit sections carry the expanding gas; and ablative liners (phenolic resin, silica-phenolic, or carbon-phenolic tape wraps) char sacrificially, shedding heat through pyrolysis gas outgassing and material recession. Moveable nozzles add a flex bearing or hydraulic actuation for thrust vector control.",
